● Hooks

  ---
  What are Hooks?

  Hooks are shell commands that automatically execute in response to specific events in Claude Code.

  They let you customize and extend Claude Code's behavior by running your own scripts at defined trigger points — without modifying Claude itself.

  ---
  How They Work

  Claude performs an action (event)
          ↓
  Hook is triggered automatically
          ↓
  Your shell command runs
          ↓
  Output fed back to Claude or logged

  ---
  Types of Hook Events

  ┌──────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┐
  │    Event     │          When it fires           │
  ├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤
  │ PreToolUse   │ Before Claude calls a tool       │
  ├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤
  │ PostToolUse  │ After a tool call completes      │
  ├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Notification │ When Claude sends a notification │
  ├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Stop         │ When Claude finishes a response  │
  ├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤
  │ SubagentStop │ When a subagent finishes         │
  └──────────────┴──────────────────────────────────┘

  ---
  Where to Configure

  Hooks are defined in Claude Code's settings file:

  ~/.claude/settings.json

  Example structure:
  {
    "hooks": {
      "PostToolUse": [
        {
          "matcher": "Bash",
          "hooks": [
            {
              "type": "command",
              "command": "echo 'Bash tool was used'"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }

  ---
  Common Use Cases

  - Logging — record every tool call Claude makes
  - Validation — block certain commands before they run
  - Notifications — alert you when Claude finishes a long task
  - Formatting — auto-format files after Claude edits them
  - Safety checks — prevent destructive commands from executing

  ---
  Key Properties

  ┌──────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ Property │                   Purpose                    │
  ├──────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ matcher  │ Which tool to watch (e.g. Bash, Edit, Write) │
  ├──────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ command  │ The shell command to run                     │
  ├──────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ type     │ Always command for now                       │
  └──────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  ---
  Core Principle

  Hooks give you control over Claude's actions — letting you observe, validate, or react to everything Claude does in your environment.


